WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:04.672
At last Miles and Edward had their day in court.

2
00:00:04.673 --> 00:00:07.991
The judge asked them to state their full names.

3
00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:11.233
"King Edward."

4
00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.058
The judge looked at Edward.

5
00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:19.224
"Would you like to try again, young man?"

6
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:24.740
Edward shook his head. "Not really."

7
00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:29.974
The judge sighed and moved on to Miles.

8
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:36.558
"And you? I suppose you're another member of the royal family?"

9
00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:39.893
"No, I'm Miles Hendon."

10
00:00:39.894 --> 00:00:44.567
The judge sighed again.

11
00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:53.269
"You do know that you're on trial for claiming to be Miles Hendon and the rightful owner of Hendon Hall?

12
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:58.238
As well as for pushing Hugh Hendon?"

13
00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:04.141
Now it was Miles' turn to sigh. "Yes."

14
00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:12.324
During the trial Hugh described Miles as a "dangerous beggar," and Miles had to be restrained from pushing him again.

15
00:01:12.325 --> 00:01:19.035
The judge sentenced Miles to sit for two hours in the stocks.

16
00:01:19.036 --> 00:01:29.105
"As for you," the judge said to Edward, "I'm tempted to give you the same punishment for being in such bad company.

17
00:01:29.106 --> 00:01:35.096
You should know better than to associate with such a rough criminal."

18
00:01:35.097 --> 00:01:40.214
"He's not a rough criminal! He's my friend and a knight—"

19
00:01:40.215 --> 00:01:44.753
"Enough!" Miles silenced Edward.

20
00:01:44.754 --> 00:01:49.033
"As I was saying," the judge said to Edward.

21
00:01:49.034 --> 00:01:52.366
"I hope you've learned your lesson.

22
00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:58.822
If I find you making trouble again, you'll go straight to the stocks."

23
00:01:58.823 --> 00:02:06.787
Edward muttered under his breath while Miles sent him frantic signals to be quiet.

24
00:02:06.788 --> 00:02:12.501
Miles was led to the stocks in the village square with Edward following along for support.

25
00:02:12.502 --> 00:02:18.043
As soon as Miles sat down, people began to mock and insult him.

26
00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:22.916
When someone hurled an egg at Miles, that was too much for Edward.

27
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:26.288
"Shame on all of you!" Edward cried.

28
00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:33.048
"This is my servant and a knight in my court. Set him free. I am—"

29
00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:36.320
"Edward, stop!" Miles shouted.

30
00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:39.357
"You'll only get yourself in trouble."

31
00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:43.025
Then he called to the sheriff, who was staring at Edward.

32
00:02:43.026 --> 00:02:47.045
"Pay no attention to the lad. He's ill."

33
00:02:47.046 --> 00:02:52.854
The sheriff approached Edward. "You need to mind your manners.

34
00:02:52.855 --> 00:02:57.162
A couple hours in the stocks might straighten you out."

35
00:02:57.163 --> 00:03:02.931
"Let's make it six," said Hugh, who had arrived to watch Miles suffer.

36
00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:07.686
The sheriff grabbed Edward and started to drag him over to the stocks.

37
00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:11.700
Edward was so shocked that he couldn't even protest.

38
00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:18.026
"Let him go!" Miles shouted. "I'll sit here for six more hours in his place."

39
00:03:18.027 --> 00:03:22.348
"No!" Edward screamed. "Don't—"

40
00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:25.542
"I'm warning you, lad," Hugh said.

41
00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:31.264
"For every word you utter, your friend will spend another hour in the stocks."

42
00:03:31.265 --> 00:03:37.427
Because of his own punishment and Edward's, Miles spent much of the day in the stocks.

43
00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:41.585
At one point Edward approached him with a small branch.

44
00:03:41.586 --> 00:03:45.054
The young king touched him lightly on each shoulder.

45
00:03:45.055 --> 00:03:49.581
"You are now an earl," Edward said to his friend.

46
00:03:49.582 --> 00:03:53.573
Miles couldn't help but smile at this honor.

47
00:03:53.574 --> 00:03:59.047
And his hours in the stocks gave him plenty of time to think about what to do next.

48
00:03:59.048 --> 00:04:02.836
"Should we return to the city?" he wondered.

49
00:04:02.837 --> 00:04:07.502
"I'm going to need someone powerful to help me before I challenge Hugh again.

50
00:04:07.503 --> 00:04:12.796
But where can I find someone like that?"

51
00:04:12.797 --> 00:04:17.203
After about four hours, Miles thought of a possibility.

52
00:04:17.204 --> 00:04:20.638
"Blake said the new king was kind and merciful.

53
00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:26.097
Maybe I could talk to him, but would he believe the word of a penniless stranger?"

54
00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:32.288
Miles thought some more. "My father had a friend at court, Sir Marlow.

55
00:04:32.289 --> 00:04:36.865
He was in charge of King Henry's kitchen or stables or something.

56
00:04:36.866 --> 00:04:39.127
Maybe he could help me.

57
00:04:39.128 --> 00:04:45.883
Yes, that's it! We'll go to the palace, and I'll ask Sir Marlow for help."

58
00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:50.877
When Miles was finally released, he was ordered to leave the village.

59
00:04:50.878 --> 00:04:56.330
He wanted to go to the palace but had second thoughts about taking Edward back to the city.

60
00:04:56.331 --> 00:05:02.347
"Edward keeps insisting on going to the coronation," Miles thought as they left the square.

61
00:05:02.348 --> 00:05:06.036
"Who knows how the excitement will affect his illness?

62
00:05:06.037 --> 00:05:09.119
What will happen when he's not crowned?"

63
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:14.170
But there was no discouraging Edward, who'd been busy planning his return.

64
00:05:14.171 --> 00:05:22.633
"By my calculations," he said happily, "we should arrive on the night before the coronation."

65
00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:25.725
And that's exactly what happened.

66
00:05:25.726 --> 00:05:31.171
Miles and Edward arrived at night to find the city already celebrating.

67
00:05:31.172 --> 00:05:35.181
But Edward hadn't anticipated what would happen next.

68
00:05:35.182 --> 00:05:41.993
As they approached the bridge, Miles and Edward lost each other in the crowd.

69
00:05:41.994 --> 00:05:47.170
Edward made his way to the cathedral where the coronation would take place.

70
00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:53.778
Dressed in rags, hungry and tired, the real king stood near the door.

71
00:05:53.779 --> 00:06:01.052
Watching workers streaming into and out of the cathedral, he waited for just the right moment.

72
00:06:01.053 --> 00:06:10.929
Then Edward slipped into the cathedral behind a carpenter and found a hiding place.

